# cluster.example — copy to input/cluster and name the doors.
#
# One line per door:
#   name host port kind
#
# The format matches the porch in gif-generator on purpose. A door is an
# address that answers; what stands behind it — one machine, three little
# minds, a split model — is not this program's business.
#
# kind is one of:
#   mirror     answers /completion, turns a meaning inside out
#   angle      answers /embedding, measures how far the turn went
#   both       answers both, because one llama-server can
#
# A door with no kind is assumed to be "both".
#
# The reader will refuse to start if a named door does not answer. It will
# not quietly fall back to running everything here — a cluster you thought
# was helping and wasn't is worse than no cluster, because the timings lie.
# If you want to read on this machine alone, say so out loud:
#
#   here 127.0.0.1 8080 both
#
# cluster-one   192.168.1.41  8080  both
# cluster-two   192.168.1.42  8080  both
# cluster-three 192.168.1.43  8080  both
# workstation   192.168.0.115 8080  mirror
# local-gpu     127.0.0.1     8080  both
